4. Battery: power-limited sizing with datasheet ratings

4.1. Power-limited inequality

The pack mass is the maximum of the energy-sized and power-sized requirements:

m_{\rm batt}
=
\max\left(
\frac{E_{\rm mission}/{\rm DoD}_{\rm usable}}{k_{\rm derate}\,e_{\rm pack}},
\;
\frac{P_{\rm hover,elec}}{\mathrm{C\!-\!rate}_{\rm cont}\,e_{\rm pack}}
\right).
\tag{14}

The second term is the formal statement of the power-limited regime. If P_{\rm hover,elec}>\mathrm{C\!-\!rate}_{\rm cont}\,e_{\rm pack}\,m_{\rm batt}^{\rm energy}, then adding energy density does not reduce pack mass; only increasing the continuous rating or reducing hover power does. The crossover is mission-dependent and is computed per case, not fixed.

4.2. Datasheet ratings of the semi-solid-state packs

The semi-solid-state packs are listed at 380 Wh/kg, but the product titles conflate peak and continuous ratings. The datasheet specifications are:

Pack Energy Max continuous Max peak
39 Ah 8S 1154.4 Wh 117 A (3C) 130 A
10.5 Ah 8S 310.8 Wh 31.5 A (3C) 90 A (\le15\ \mathrm{s})

The continuous rating is 3C for both packs. The “10C” label on the 10.5 Ah product refers to its peak rating, not to a continuous rating. Using 10C as a continuous design value would violate Eq. (14) and under-size the power pack. The dual-pack architecture is therefore retained as a peak-shaving arrangement, not as a continuous-power solution:

· the 10.5 Ah pack supplies the take-off and climb transient at up to 90 A for \le15\ \mathrm{s};
· the 39 Ah pack supplies the sustained cruise and hover energy at 3C continuous.

The two packs are paralleled through ideal-diode isolation, with an active cooling duct in the peripheral ring. This satisfies Eq. (14) without oversizing the energy pack, but it does not raise the continuous rating above 3C.

4.3. Derating

The 39 Ah pack retains \ge80\% capacity after 300+ cycles; the 10.5 Ah pack retains \ge80\% after 300+ cycles, per datasheet. The screening derating k_{\rm derate}=0.80 is retained until an enclosure thermal soak at 45\ ^\circ\mathrm{C} ambient is performed [S]. It is a conservative screening value, not a thermal model, and it is not a measured result.

