Appendix G — Architecture description

G.1. Structural architecture

A carbon-composite central torsion box carries the payload platform and the battery bays. Four propulsion arms are bonded to the torsion box and terminate in motor mounts. A peripheral ring defines the carpet silhouette and carries three landing skids. The ring is bending-and-torsion dominated and is carried as a separate mass term m_{\rm ring} because its scaling law differs from the chassis.

