Appendix K — Closure solver algorithm

```
INPUT: m_payload, N_r, D, e_pack, k_derate, DoD, f_struct,
       eta chain, V, d, t_hover, f(theta), C_d0, sigma, kappa(mu)

1  Set M^(0) = m_payload / 0.25        # seeding, no physical meaning
2  repeat
3      A_tot   = N_r * pi * (D/2)^2
4      DL      = M^(k) * g / A_tot
5      if DL > 150: flag Class B/C; break
6      P_hov   = (M^(k) g)^(3/2) / sqrt(2 rho A_tot) / eta_Sigma
7      P_cru   = f(chi, V, f, C_d0, sigma, eta_prop, eta_Sigma)
8      E_mis   = P_hov * t_hover + P_cru * (2d/V)
9      m_E     = E_mis / DoD / (k_derate * e_pack)
10     m_P     = P_hov / (C_cont * e_pack)
11     m_batt  = max(m_E, m_P)
12     m_prop  = c_p * N_r * (D/2)^2
13     M^(k+1) = m_payload + m_batt + m_prop
                 + f_struct * M^(k) + m_av + m_lg + m_env
14     L = f_struct + dm_batt/dM + dm_prop/dM
15 until |M^(k+1) - M^(k)| < tol  and  L < 1
16 M*    = M^(k+1)
17 M_MTOW = 1.12 * M*
18 report M*, M_MTOW, L, branch(m_E vs m_P), screens satisfied
```

Convergence is not feasibility. A converged M^{*} that violates any screen of Appendix J is reported as Class B.

