Appendix P — Epistemic boundary

This appendix states explicitly what the blueprint does not claim:

1. No mass has been measured. M^{*} is a fixed point of a model, not a weighing result.
2. No endurance has been measured. Mission energy in Appendix E is computed from assumed efficiencies and an assumed f.
3. No thrust stand, no thermal soak, no wind-tunnel test, and no static load test has been performed.
4. No prototype, partial or complete, exists.
5. No flight has occurred.
6. The efficiency values in Eq. (C.1) are literature-sourced, not measured on this configuration.
7. The battery ratings in Appendix E are datasheet values, not values measured inside the ring enclosure.
8. The layout footprints in Appendix F are geometric calculations, not built hardware.
9. The regulatory statements in Appendix O are readings of published and draft texts, not legal advice and not a certification determination.
10. The contraction condition L<1 is verified numerically inside the solver for specific parameter sets; it is not proved analytically for all admissible parameter sets.

